  "full_text": "So, like, just looking at my hands, you know. Been doing that a lot. And I can feel it in my fingers, you know. And, you know, my penmanship's not real good. You know, some people are surgeons. Some people are surgeons. Some people are fighter pilots. Hard to say. I wonder what I'm adapted for. I'm a drummer. I don't know if that, uh, I don't know if that's innate or, uh, or, uh, I got like, uh, I got four clocks. Watch this. Let's see. I got four, uh, independent, uh, clocks in my, uh, limbs, right? Watch this. Let's check this shit out. Uh, four independent clocks. Or not four. Well, yeah. Well, I don't know if that's just from drumming or what. It's like, uh, Not doing it real good there, but I'm pretty good about that. I think I can do an impressive independent clock motion, you know. You know, I trained with... Drywall was my karate kid. You know, the other thing was bagging groceries. I asked God, hey, God, what did bagging groceries give me? He said it gave me speed. And with... More of a sense of urgency, like you rush through all your work, like you go to university, you rush, rush, rush, you know, you're in a hurry all the time. So like, it gives you a rush, rush, rush in everything. Probably sloppy, but rush, rush, rush, you know?",
